<%# What a run was asked to do, and what came back.
    A task is a whole brief — two kilobytes is ordinary — so the row that reads
    it cannot: the line says the beginning, and this is where the rest of it is
    read. Opened by tapping the row, because the tooltip it used to hide in is
    not a control a phone has (see `_subagent_rows`).

    `run` is either a background run from SubagentJobs (task/result/error) or a
    transcript item (task only): a finished turn records what was asked, not the
    answer, which the turn's own text already carries. -%>
<dl class="subagent-brief">
<% if run[:task].to_s != "" -%>
  <dt><%= h(I18n.t("web.subagents.prompt")) %></dt>
  <dd><pre class="subagent-brief-text"><%= h(run[:task]) %></pre></dd>
<% end -%>
<% if run[:result].to_s != "" -%>
  <dt><%= h(I18n.t("web.subagents.result")) %></dt>
  <dd><pre class="subagent-brief-text"><%= h(run[:result]) %></pre></dd>
<% end -%>
<% if run[:error].to_s != "" -%>
  <dt><%= h(I18n.t("web.subagents.error")) %></dt>
  <dd><pre class="subagent-brief-text subagent-brief-error"><%= h(run[:error]) %></pre></dd>
<% end -%>
</dl>
